Sval: a crash report never holds the address of a page

Gecko records the address being loaded as the URL annotation: the selected
tab's in the parent, each load's in its content process, and each
transaction's in the GPU process. It does so in private windows too. A crash
writes every annotation to the report's .extra file, where it stays, and
about:crashes posts it with the report. Sval keeps and sends nothing that
says what the user is browsing, so the annotation is gone from
CrashAnnotations.yaml, which makes any code that records it fail to compile
or throw, and so are its writers. The boxes that offered to include the
address, in the crash reporter window and on about:tabcrashed, go with it.

